{% comment %}
  Local override of al_folio_core/_includes/footer.liquid.

  Why this exists: upstream renders an unconditional copyright bar
  ("© Copyright <year> <name>. <footer_text>"). It has no config flag — neither
  `footer_text` nor `footer_fixed` can suppress it — so the only way to drop it
  is to shadow the include.

  What changed: nothing is rendered. The page simply ends after the content.

  Upstream reference (al_folio_core 1.0.15):
    {% capture footer_contents %}
      &copy; Copyright {{ site.time | date: '%Y' }}
      {{ site.first_name }} {{ site.middle_name }} {{ site.last_name }}. {{ site.footer_text }}
      ...
    {% endcapture %}
    {% if site.footer_fixed %}
      <footer class="fixed-bottom" role="contentinfo"> ...
    {% else %}
      <footer class="sticky-bottom mt-5" role="contentinfo"> ...
    {% endif %}

  To restore: delete this file. To reinstate a minimal footer instead, render a
  <footer> element with just {{ site.footer_text }}.

  Note: `body` carries `padding-bottom: 70px` whenever `footer_fixed: true`, so
  the page keeps a little breathing room below the content. That is intentional.

  Acknowledged in .al-folio-overrides.yml via:
    bundle exec al-folio upgrade overrides accept _includes/footer.liquid
{% endcomment %}